# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local configuration holding real data paths and imaging-archive identifiers.
# Only the *_example.py templates are committed; never a filled-in copy.
# Matched at any depth, so the rules survive a component moving.
**/config/local*
!**/config/local_example.py
**/config/*_private*

# Solver working directories created by the calibration loops
run_iter*/
iteration_*/

# Output of the synthetic phantom generator: ~200 MB of meshes and one array,
# all of it reproduced exactly by running make_phantom.py. The generator is what
# is distributed, which is also the clearer provenance argument. The pre-commit
# guard refuses these extensions in any case.
**/examples/phantom/data/

# Anything the tracking-step validation notebooks write when they are run.
**/tracking-validation/data/

# Everything that belongs to preparing the deposit rather than to the deposit:
# the internal design record, correspondence drafts, and the files that arrived
# as attachments. What arrives this way gets read, integrated where it belongs,
# and recorded — the raw material is not itself deposit material.
#
# One directory rather than a rule per file, so that the boundary is visible on
# disk and nothing new has to be remembered.
/internal/

# Kept as well, so that a draft or an attachment dropped outside internal/ by
# habit is still refused.
email-*.md
**/Rodrigo/
